small pupil and on the

246
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:13,030
same size have same
side, have a droopy upper

247
00:10:13,030 --> 00:10:15,190
lid. They may have a
lack of sweating on

248
00:10:15,190 --> 00:10:17,710
the forehead above
the affected eye. And

249
00:10:17,710 --> 00:10:19,630
there's different
ideologies for this. It can

250
00:10:19,630 --> 00:10:21,620
be something called
preganglionic, which

251
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:23,530
extends anywhere from
the hypothalamus to the

252
00:10:23,530 --> 00:10:25,790
superior cervical
ganglion, which is

253
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:28,150
usually from ******,
though it can be from a

254
00:10:28,150 --> 00:10:30,150
vertebral artery dissection
and cervical disc

255
00:10:30,150 --> 00:10:33,050
disease. And it can
also originate from a

256
00:10:33,050 --> 00:10:35,890
postganglionic source.
And the most common

257
00:10:35,890 --> 00:10:37,810
and severe thing that
we worry about here

258
00:10:37,810 --> 00:10:40,550
is internal carotid
artery dissection, which

259
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:43,510
can not only cause
****** and this syndrome,

260
00:10:43,510 --> 00:10:47,830
but other problems as
well. So any person

261
00:10:47,830 --> 00:10:50,070
that you suspect has
Horner's syndrome

262
00:10:50,070 --> 00:10:52,130
should have a neural
workup to make sure that

263
00:10:52,130 --> 00:10:53,850
there's nothing that
we're missing here.

264
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:57,750
Just some more pupils.
There's something

265
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:59,190
called a Hutchinson's
pupil, where

266
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:00,950
there's a unilaterally
dilated poorly

267
00:11:00,950 --> 00:11:03,390
reactive patient pupil
and a comatose patient.

268
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:06,310
And this is usually
due to um, um,

269
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,430
uncle herniation
or displacement

270
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:09,970
of the hippocampal
gyrus, which

271
00:11:09,970 --> 00:11:11,890
entraps the third
cranial nerve.

272
00:11:13,330 --> 00:11:16,610
There's also other
ocular muscle disorders,

273
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:18,890
chronic, chronic
progressive external

274
00:11:18,890 --> 00:11:21,110
ophthalmoplegia
or CPEO, which is

275
00:11:21,110 --> 00:11:23,950
a mitochondrial
disease. Um, it can be

276
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:25,310
associated with
something called Kieran

277
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:27,970
-Seres syndrome, where
there's a retinal

278
00:11:27,970 --> 00:11:29,870
pigment degeneration
and heart block.

279
00:11:29,870 --> 00:11:31,870
Myasthenia gravis
is probably the most

280
00:11:31,870 --> 00:11:33,570
common ocular muscle
disorder that'll

281
00:11:33,570 --> 00:11:35,890
pop up in life and
also on the boards,

282
00:11:35,890 --> 00:11:37,650
where there's weakness
of the voluntary

283
00:11:37,650 --> 00:11:40,510
muscles due to
autoimmunity up to the

284
00:11:40,510 --> 00:11:42,310
motor end plate.
So basically, the

285
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:46,210
acetylcholine receptor
have antibodies that

286
00:11:46,210 --> 00:11:47,730
are floating around
and blocking them.

287
00:11:47,930 --> 00:11:50,270
So the most common
thing is patients just

288
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:54,410
have severe weakness.
Usually, you see it's

289
00:11:54,410 --> 00:11:57,010
fatigability. So
patients might say, I

290
00:11:57,010 --> 00:11:58,390
wake up in the morning
and things are okay,

291
00:11:58,390 --> 00:12:00,430
and as the day goes
on, I'm just so weak.

292
00:12:00,430 --> 00:12:02,950
90% of these patients
with myasthenia do

293
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:05,370
have eye symptoms.
so they might have

294
00:12:05,370 --> 00:12:07,190
eye fatigue, they
might have ptosis, they

295
00:12:07,190 --> 00:12:08,650
might have diplopia,
they might have

296
00:12:08,650 --> 00:12:10,850
limitation of their
extraocular movement.

297
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:14,290
And there are some
patients that have

298
00:12:14,290 --> 00:12:17,270
only ocular myasthenia
where this is limited

299
00:12:17,270 --> 00:12:20,070
just to the eyes.
The diagnosis is

300
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:22,530
typically done by a
neurologist but usually

301
00:12:22,530 --> 00:12:24,250
they use something
called a tensilon test

302
00:12:24,250 --> 00:12:27,490
which is something
that's injected

303
00:12:27,490 --> 00:12:30,780
through the IV, and it's
acetylcholinesterase

304
00:12:31,190 --> 00:12:33,610
inhibitor, so it
prolongs the action of

305
00:12:33,610 --> 00:12:36,310
acetylcholine, and it
produces a stronger

306
00:12:36,310 --> 00:12:38,250
muscle contraction
in these patients.

307
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:40,730
Another way of testing
this is testing

308
00:12:40,730 --> 00:12:42,910
for the acetylcholine
receptor antibodies

309
00:12:42,910 --> 00:12:44,970
for binding, blocking,
and modulating.

310
00:12:46,830 --> 00:12:48,910
There's other ocular
muscle disorders

311
00:12:48,910 --> 00:12:50,950
that we might see
too, such as thyroid

312
00:12:50,950 --> 00:12:52,970
-related ophthalmopathy.
You may have seen

313
00:12:52,970 --> 00:12:54,670
commercials for
thyroid eye disease.

314
00:12:55,310 --> 00:12:58,470
typically what happens
here is there is

315
00:12:58,470 --> 00:13:02,810
deposition of these
autoimmune particles within

316
00:13:02,810 --> 00:13:05,970
the tissue surrounding
the orbit. And you

317
00:13:05,970 --> 00:13:07,790
get a lot of congestion
in the orbit and

318
00:13:07,790 --> 00:13:09,950
proptosis where the
eyes are pushed forward.

319
00:13:09,950 --> 00:13:12,590
So the eyelids become
retracted, as you see

320
00:13:12,590 --> 00:13:14,890
in the picture here
on the left-hand side.

321
00:13:15,010 --> 00:13:17,490
The patients can
have dry eye redness

322
00:13:17,490 --> 00:13:19,910
and pain, restriction
of motility. They

323
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:21,990
even can have optic
nerve compression.

324
00:13:21,990 --> 00:13:24,010
And the tricky thing
with this is that

325
00:13:24,010 --> 00:13:25,830
they may actually
have normal thyroid

326
00:13:25,830 --> 00:13:28,890
levels, but they
typically do have the

327
00:13:28,890 --> 00:13:31,630
antibodies for thyroid
disease present.

328
00:13:31,910 --> 00:13:34,030
Another ocular
muscle disorder

329
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:35,510
is myotonic dystrophy.

330
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:38,090
It is autosomal
dominant from chromosome

331
00:13:38,090 --> 00:13:41,830
19. And these patients
have myotonia of

332
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:44,650
the peripheral muscles.
They can have very

333
00:13:44,650 --> 00:13:45,970
interesting looking
cataracts called

334
00:13:45,970 --> 00:13:48,070
Christmas tree cataracts,
which we see here.

335
00:13:49,670 --> 00:13:52,510
There's other vascular
optic neuropathies.

336
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:54,730
The two main ones
that we need to know

337
00:13:54,730 --> 00:13:56,090
about are something
called anterior

338
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:59,270
ischemic optic neuropathy,
or AION, and posterior

339
00:13:59,270 --> 00:14:01,550
ischemic optic
neuropathy, or PION.

340
00:14:02,870 --> 00:14:05,250
Anterior ischemic
optic neuropathy has to

341
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:07,450
do with an infarct of
the optic nerve head

342
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:09,790
just posterior to
the lamina curbrosa,

343
00:14:09,790 --> 00:14:12,770
and this causes an
acute painless vision

344
00:14:12,770 --> 00:14:14,730
loss. So patients
come in saying, I just

345
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:17,680
lost vision, but
there's no opinion. They

346
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:20,390
typically do have an
RAPD. They typically

347
00:14:20,390 --> 00:14:23,310
do have some finding
of the optic nerve

348
00:14:23,310 --> 00:14:25,190
on exam where there
might be optic disc

349
00:14:25,190 --> 00:14:26,710
edema, which you can
kind of see in the

350
00:14:26,710 --> 00:14:28,450
pictures down below. It
looks like there's this

351
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:32,090
fuzziness surrounding
the optic nerve.

352
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:36,490
And what we worry
about in AION is if

353
00:14:36,490 --> 00:14:38,490
it's inflammatory
because that's something

354
00:14:38,490 --> 00:14:41,290
called arteritic
ION or giant cell

355
00:14:41,290 --> 00:14:43,770
arteritis or temporal
arteritis. And the

356
00:14:43,770 --> 00:14:46,250
issue with this is
that it affects medium

357
00:14:46,250 --> 00:14:49,450
to large size
vessels. And there can

358
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:52,170
be vision loss in one
eye and very acute

359
00:14:52,170 --> 00:14:53,950
vision loss to follow
that in the other

360
00:14:53,950 --> 00:14:55,810
eye. So it has to
be detected early.

361
00:14:56,950 --> 00:14:59,090
The non-artertic
ischemic optic

362
00:14:59,090 --> 00:15:01,130
neuropathy is
typically associated

363
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:02,790
with microvascular
disease.

364
00:15:02,990 --> 00:15:05,090
Posterior ischemic
optic neuropathy has a

365
00:15:05,090 --> 00:15:07,030
lot to do with
decreased blood flow and

366
00:15:07,030 --> 00:15:09,990
oxygenation into the
intraorbital optic nerve.

367
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:13,650
So more on giant
cell arteritis.

368
00:15:13,650 --> 00:15:15,710
This is tested a lot
both on ophthalmic

369
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:18,310
and regular boards.
So again, it's

370
00:15:18,310 --> 00:15:19,770
an inflammatory
vasculopathy

371
00:15:19,770 --> 00:15:22,010
affecting medium to
large size vessels.

372
00:15:22,190 --> 00:15:25,090
Typically, the presentation
is an older male

373
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:28,290
or female, older
than 55. They come in

374
00:15:28,290 --> 00:15:31,190
complaining of a headache
on one side, decreased

375
00:15:31,190 --> 00:15:34,190
vision. They may have
double vision. They

376
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:36,930
may also have scalp
tenderness. They may get

377
00:15:36,930 --> 00:15:40,790
jaw pain or pain or
fatigue ability of the

378
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:43,450
jaw when they're chewing.
They may have new

379
00:15:43,450 --> 00:15:47,490
onset pain or arthritis
like pain in their

380
00:15:47,490 --> 00:15:50,950
shoulders or their hip
area. And when you do

381
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:54,330
an exam, you sometimes
can see an RIPD on

382
00:15:54,330 --> 00:15:58,310
that side. You sometimes
can see a fuzzy

383
00:15:58,310 --> 00:16:01,350
looking or a pale or
edematous optic nerve on

384
00:16:01,350 --> 00:16:04,730
that side. And you may
actually feel a decreased

385
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:07,150
pulsation of the
temporal artery on that

386
00:16:07,150 --> 00:16:10,370
side compared to the
other side. So if you're

387
00:16:10,370 --> 00:16:13,550
suspecting this, the
typical workup is to

388
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:16,630
get blood work first
and you may see an

389
00:16:16,630 --> 00:16:19,750
elevated ESR or an
erythrocyte sedimentation

390
00:16:19,750 --> 00:16:23,030
rate, a CRP, which is
a C-reactive protein.

391
00:16:23,030 --> 00:16:26,010
You may also see a low
hematocrit, and you

392
00:16:26,010 --> 00:16:28,060
may also see elevated
platelet levels or

393
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:31,750
thrombocytosis. Any
elevation in these with a

394
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:34,590
corresponding clinical
picture that's suspicious

395
00:16:34,590 --> 00:16:37,990
for temporal arteritis
should have a workup

396
00:16:37,990 --> 00:16:41,290
with a rheumatology
partner and also will

397
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:43,590
likely need a temporal
artery biopsy to

398
00:16:43,590 --> 00:16:46,790
confirm the diagnosis.
We usually start steroids

399
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:49,110
for these patients,
oral or IV, depending

400
00:16:49,110 --> 00:16:53,330
on how severe the
presentation is, to prevent

401
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:55,830
basically vision loss
in the fellow eye

402
00:16:55,830 --> 00:16:58,010
because whatever vision
loss has occurred in

403
00:16:58,010 --> 00:17:00,830
the presenting eye may
not be retrievable,

404
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:03,850
but we want to make sure
that the inflammation

405
00:17:03,850 --> 00:17:06,530
doesn't continue on
within the body and

406
00:17:06,530 --> 00:17:08,670
go on to affect the
vision in the other eye.

407
00:17:10,050 --> 00:17:12,610
There's also, in
terms of other optic

408
00:17:12,610 --> 00:17:14,490
neuropathy, is something
called idiopathic

409
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:17,170
intracranial hypertension
or pseudotumor, which

410
00:17:17,170 --> 00:17:20,190
you see here a very
edematous optic nerve

411
00:17:20,190 --> 00:17:24,410
with normal neuroimaging
and normal CSF

412
00:17:24,410 --> 00:17:27,770
findings if you were
to do a lumbar puncture

413
00:17:27,770 --> 00:17:30,050
and look at the cell
types in the CSF,

414
00:17:30,050 --> 00:17:32,930
the cerebral spinal
fluid. Usually this is

415
00:17:32,930 --> 00:17:35,610
in female patients
around age 33 or younger.

416
00:17:35,610 --> 00:17:37,730
It is associated
with obesity. These

417
00:17:37,730 --> 00:17:39,830
patients typically have
really severe headaches,

418
00:17:39,830 --> 00:17:41,910
nausea, vomiting,
optic disc edema. They

419
00:17:41,910 --> 00:17:43,630
may have something
called transient visual

420
00:17:43,630 --> 00:17:46,730
obscurations where
they go from a sitting

421
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:48,510
to standing position
or a laying down to

422
00:17:48,510 --> 00:17:50,810
a sitting position
and they lose vision

423
00:17:50,810 --> 00:17:53,170
and then it comes back.
They may have something

424
00:17:53,170 --> 00:17:56,810
called pulsatile
tinnitus as well, where

425
00:17:56,810 --> 00:17:58,290
they hear almost like
a whooshing sound

426
00:17:58,290 --> 00:18:01,590
in their ears along
with the vision loss.

427
00:18:03,390 --> 00:18:07,450
So it can be due to
durosinous thrombosis.

428
00:18:07,450 --> 00:18:09,130
It can be due to
use of steroids. It

429
00:18:09,130 --> 00:18:11,600
can be due to use of
oral contraceptives,

430
00:18:12,030 --> 00:18:13,970
vitamin A toxicity,

431
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:16,390
and iso-retinoin
toxicity.

432
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,930
The treatment
is an escalating

433
00:18:18,930 --> 00:18:20,610
treatment. So if
these patients have no

434
00:18:20,610 --> 00:18:22,790
vision loss, we
just basically treat

435
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:24,970
their headaches
and weight loss is

436
00:18:24,970 --> 00:18:26,970
advised, which
typically helps a lot.

437
00:18:27,050 --> 00:18:29,930
Mild vision loss, we do
give something called

438
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:32,170
acetazolamide, which
is a diuretic, which

439
00:18:32,170 --> 00:18:33,890
helps to decrease
the symptoms as well

440
00:18:33,890 --> 00:18:35,750
as weight loss. And
if the vision loss is

441
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:38,430
very, very advanced,
these patients may need

442
00:18:38,430 --> 00:18:40,530
serial lumbar puncture
and something called

443
00:18:40,530 --> 00:18:43,170
a lumboparitoneal
shunt or an LP shunt.

444
00:18:44,510 --> 00:18:46,830
Optic neuritis
is another optic

445
00:18:46,830 --> 00:18:48,370
neuropathy to be
aware of. It's

446
00:18:48,370 --> 00:18:50,070
inflammation of
the optic nerve.

447
00:18:50,070 --> 00:18:52,270
It's the most common
optic neuropathy

448
00:18:52,270 --> 00:18:53,990
in patients younger
than 45 years

449
00:18:53,990 --> 00:18:55,730
old. And these patients
may also present

450
00:18:55,730 --> 00:18:57,710
with acute unilateral
vision loss,

451
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:59,650
and it may recover
spontaneously.

452
00:18:59,730 --> 00:19:01,350
They typically
have pain and eye

453
00:19:01,350 --> 00:19:03,650
movement. They typically
do have an RAPD

454
00:19:03,650 --> 00:19:05,690
with a visual field
defect. The optic

455
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:07,870
nerve can appeal
normal or swollen.

456
00:19:07,990 --> 00:19:10,230
These patients can
have something called

457
00:19:10,230 --> 00:19:12,050
UTOF's phenomenon where
they have worsening

458
00:19:12,050 --> 00:19:13,970
of their symptoms
with heat or exercise.

459
00:19:14,770 --> 00:19:17,150
And the thing that
we need to remember

460
00:19:17,150 --> 00:19:19,210
with optic neuritis
is that 30% of these

461
00:19:19,210 --> 00:19:21,070
patients can develop
MS within four

462
00:19:21,070 --> 00:19:24,610
years and 38% within
10 years. So this is

463
00:19:24,610 --> 00:19:27,030
not something that
even if it goes away,

464
00:19:27,030 --> 00:19:28,590
we're like, okay,
we're done. We can

465
00:19:28,590 --> 00:19:29,990
move on. We always
have to be watching

466
00:19:29,990 --> 00:19:32,310
these patients
neurologically as well.

467
00:19:33,390 --> 00:19:35,850
So that was our basically

468
00:19:35,850 --> 00:19:37,830
basic science
ophthalmology.

469
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:40,350
We're going to move
on to more clinical

470
00:19:40,350 --> 00:19:42,450
ophthalmology and what
we would typically see

471
00:19:42,450 --> 00:19:44,810
for patients who come
into the ER or the office

472
00:19:44,810 --> 00:19:47,050
and things that pop
up on boards as well.

473
00:19:47,790 --> 00:19:49,990
So ocular disease,
the thing to be aware

474
00:19:49,990 --> 00:19:52,010
of is it can be
isolated to one or both

475
00:19:52,010 --> 00:19:54,130
eyes, and it can be
related to systemic

476
00:19:54,130 --> 00:19:56,210
conditions, which we'll
see going forward.

477
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:01,310
So big thing here
is the red eye. This

478
00:20:01,310 --> 00:20:03,490
comes in to urgent
care, comes into the

479
00:20:03,490 --> 00:20:05,850
ER, comes into the
office. It's everywhere,

480
00:20:05,850 --> 00:20:07,330
and there's many
different cause.

481
00:20:07,530 --> 00:20:11,130
So from outside to
in, the red eyelids.

482
00:20:11,130 --> 00:20:12,870
You can have something
called blepharitis,

483
00:20:12,870 --> 00:20:15,550
which is simply
dryness and irritation

484
00:20:15,550 --> 00:20:18,470
of the eyelids
where the lash line

485
00:20:18,470 --> 00:20:20,730
is, and that can cause
dry eye symptoms.

486
00:20:20,830 --> 00:20:24,010
You can have the stye,
which is basically

487
00:20:24,030 --> 00:20:26,130
a clogging of the oil
glands on the external

488
00:20:26,130 --> 00:20:27,630
part of the eyelid.
You can have a

489
00:20:27,630 --> 00:20:29,930
chalazin, which is
almost like a stye that's

490
00:20:29,930 --> 00:20:31,730
just deeper within
the eyelid, but it can

491
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:33,830
be a little bit harder
to treat. Typically,

492
00:20:33,830 --> 00:20:35,770
these have to be
incised and drained.

493
00:20:36,650 --> 00:20:39,140
And you can have
something called preceptal

494
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:40,610
cellulitis, where
you get a cellulitis

495
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:42,630
of the tissue
surrounding the eye.

496
00:20:45,470 --> 00:20:48,950
Another part of a red
eyelid situation is

497
00:20:48,950 --> 00:20:50,930
something called ******
zoster ophthalmicus,

498
00:20:50,930 --> 00:20:52,970
where you can have a
****** zoster infection

499
00:20:52,970 --> 00:20:57,770
involving the V1
distribution of the

500
00:20:57,770 --> 00:21:01,650
face. So you can see this
rash along the forehead

501
00:21:01,650 --> 00:21:04,290
and along the nose
on that side. And it

502
00:21:04,290 --> 00:21:06,310
can typically is very
red and it has other

503
00:21:06,310 --> 00:21:08,290
lesions that scab over
similar to chicken

504
00:21:08,290 --> 00:21:10,730
pox. And you can also
have something that's

505
00:21:10,730 --> 00:21:13,690
orbital cellulitis
where the preceptal

506
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:15,250
cellulitis picture that
you see in the lower

507
00:21:15,250 --> 00:21:19,090
here has progressed to
go behind the globe.

508
00:21:19,230 --> 00:21:22,890
And these are usually
children who get this,

509
00:21:22,890 --> 00:21:25,330
but they present
with very, very tense

510
00:21:25,330 --> 00:21:27,290
eyelids. It's almost
impossible to open the

511
00:21:27,290 --> 00:21:30,030
eyelid. And when you do
a CT scan, you see that

512
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:32,730
