515
00:21:38,390 --> 00:21:41,170
So back to ******
osteophthalmicus, this

516
00:21:41,170 --> 00:21:43,530
is a big one that
basically all practitioners

517
00:21:43,530 --> 00:21:45,290
have to be aware
of what it looks

518
00:21:45,290 --> 00:21:47,490
like. comes into the
ER, comes into the

519
00:21:47,490 --> 00:21:49,930
office, comes into
urgent care. It's a

520
00:21:49,930 --> 00:21:52,130
unilateral painful skin
rash and a dermatonal

521
00:21:52,130 --> 00:21:54,050
distribution of the
trigeminal nerve.

522
00:21:54,270 --> 00:21:56,850
It presents with vesicles
on the skin, which

523
00:21:56,850 --> 00:21:58,890
typically crust and
heal within two to six

524
00:21:58,890 --> 00:22:01,570
weeks. And if a patient
has Hutchinson's side

525
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:03,370
where there's skin
lesions at the tip side

526
00:22:03,370 --> 00:22:05,390
or root of the nose,
there's a strong, strong

527
00:22:05,390 --> 00:22:07,090
predictor of ocular
involvement because

528
00:22:07,090 --> 00:22:09,390
this is where the
nasoaciliary nerve travels.

529
00:22:09,510 --> 00:22:12,490
So the issue with
this is that this is

530
00:22:12,490 --> 00:22:14,910
not just having
vesicles on the eyelid.

531
00:22:14,910 --> 00:22:17,270
These patients can
actually have a ******

532
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:18,830
zoster infection
of their eyeball

533
00:22:18,830 --> 00:22:20,670
itself, which can
sometimes be very, very

534
00:22:20,670 --> 00:22:22,770
difficult to
treat. It typically

535
00:22:22,770 --> 00:22:25,710
presents an adult older
than 60 years old,

536
00:22:26,030 --> 00:22:28,790
and it's basically
a reactivation of

537
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:31,130
latent varicella
zoster virus in the

538
00:22:31,130 --> 00:22:33,850
sensory spine or
cerebral ganglia.

539
00:22:34,010 --> 00:22:36,530
It can be more
prevalent in

