to manage that pain.

558
00:23:29,790 --> 00:23:33,070
Moving forward, there's
also the red eyeballs.

559
00:23:33,070 --> 00:23:34,610
So we did the red
eyelids. Now there's

560
00:23:34,610 --> 00:23:36,190
red eyeballs. There's
many different kinds

561
00:23:36,190 --> 00:23:38,270
of conjunctivitis or
pink eye. It can be

562
00:23:38,270 --> 00:23:41,150
allergic, contact,
inflammatory, infectious.

563
00:23:41,750 --> 00:23:44,070
We can also have a
redness just because

564
00:23:44,070 --> 00:23:46,010
of something called
subconjunctival hemorrhage,

565
00:23:46,010 --> 00:23:47,190
where a small
blood vessel on the

566
00:23:47,190 --> 00:23:49,410
surface of the eye
bursts. And it can look

567
00:23:49,410 --> 00:23:51,230
very, very red, but
it goes away on its

568
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:53,530
own, and it's really
of not a consequence.

569
00:23:53,530 --> 00:23:55,730
And the lower picture
here is just a

570
00:23:55,730 --> 00:23:57,450
picture of what's called
episcleritis, where

571
00:23:57,450 --> 00:23:59,430
it's an inflammation
of the deeper layers

572
00:23:59,430 --> 00:24:01,770
of the eye rather
than the conjunctiva.

573
00:24:02,930 --> 00:24:05,970
So many, many
different ideologies

574
00:24:05,970 --> 00:24:07,930
of conjunctivitis
or pinkeye.

575
00:24:07,930 --> 00:24:09,850
Viral is the most
common cause.

576
00:24:10,010 --> 00:24:12,590
Usually adenovirus is
what we see, especially

577
00:24:12,590 --> 00:24:14,550
this time of year.
We have like a watery

578
00:24:14,550 --> 00:24:16,830
discharge with that,
eyelid swelling. You

579
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:19,350
can get ******
infections that can cause

580
00:24:19,350 --> 00:24:21,830
just a conjunctivitis
picture. These are

581
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:24,530
typically treated
symptomatically as they do

582
00:24:24,530 --> 00:24:26,110
resolve on their own,
although some patients

583
00:24:26,110 --> 00:24:28,410
may need antiviral
treatments. We can have

584
00:24:28,410 --> 00:24:30,530
allergic conjunctivitis,
which is treated

585
00:24:30,530 --> 00:24:33,070
usually with topical
allergy medications

586
00:24:33,070 --> 00:24:37,030
or oral bacterial
conjunctivitis. Usually,

587
00:24:37,030 --> 00:24:40,130
this is seen more in
children. We get a pus,

588
00:24:40,130 --> 00:24:42,490
mucousy kind of
discharge, and it usually

589
00:24:42,490 --> 00:24:44,770
lasts a week to 10
days, and these are

590
00:24:44,770 --> 00:24:47,390
definitely treated with
antibiotic eye drops.

591
00:24:48,790 --> 00:24:52,310
Gonorrhea is actually
something that we

592
00:24:52,310 --> 00:24:54,490
always look out for
because it can actually

593
00:24:54,490 --> 00:24:56,850
become so severe,
it can perforate the

594
00:24:56,850 --> 00:24:58,930
cornea. So these
patients are typically

595
00:24:58,930 --> 00:25:02,650
given a dose of
intramuscular ceftriaxone.

596
00:25:03,790 --> 00:25:06,050
And believe it
or not, COVID can

597
00:25:06,050 --> 00:25:08,650
present with pinkeye
as well. So things

598
00:25:08,650 --> 00:25:11,050
to be aware of as
you see all these

599
00:25:11,050 --> 00:25:13,330
patients with pinkeye
in your careers.

600
00:25:16,030 --> 00:25:18,790
Scleritis basically
involves an inflammation

601
00:25:18,790 --> 00:25:21,410
of the sclera. So it's
very different than

602
00:25:21,410 --> 00:25:23,450
conjunctivitis.
Conjunctivitis, you can

603
00:25:23,450 --> 00:25:26,130
see going back here,
it's kind of like a

604
00:25:26,130 --> 00:25:29,110
lightish pink color. It
can be diffusely red,

605
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:32,450
but when you get scleritis
or even episcleritis,

606
00:25:32,450 --> 00:25:33,930
which is just the
layer of tissue

607
00:25:33,930 --> 00:25:37,110
above the sclera, it's
this deeper red, almost

608
00:25:37,110 --> 00:25:40,090
like burgundy red
that you see. And it's

609
00:25:40,090 --> 00:25:44,250
a very, very painful
experience for the

610
00:25:44,250 --> 00:25:46,670
patients. It could be
autoimmune, infectious.

611
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:49,430
It can be related to
uveitis as well, which

612
00:25:49,430 --> 00:25:51,510
is just a general
inflammation in the eye.

613
00:25:51,710 --> 00:25:54,330
You can also get a
red eyeball from a

614
00:25:54,330 --> 00:25:56,010
corneal ulcer, which
you can see on the

615
00:25:56,010 --> 00:25:59,790
top picture there.
That round grayish ring

616
00:25:59,790 --> 00:26:02,790
on the cornea is
an ulcer. And the

617
00:26:02,790 --> 00:26:04,870
white stuff that you
see in the eye is

618
00:26:04,870 --> 00:26:06,950
actually fibrin. It's
called a hypopion. So

619
00:26:06,950 --> 00:26:08,950
this is a really
severe infection that

620
00:26:09,590 --> 00:26:11,750
basically all these
white cells have

621
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:13,830
just accumulated in
the front of the eye.

622
00:26:14,530 --> 00:26:16,370
The bottom picture
shows something

623
00:26:16,370 --> 00:26:18,210
called endophthalmitis,
which is an

624
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:20,330
infection that has
spread beyond the cornea

625
00:26:20,330 --> 00:26:22,010
into all of the
layers of the eye.

626
00:26:22,010 --> 00:26:24,190
You can't even see
the pupil there.

627
00:26:24,450 --> 00:26:26,730
Typically, these
patients do need surgery

628
00:26:26,730 --> 00:26:28,910
or injections of
medication into the eye.

629
00:26:31,770 --> 00:26:33,970
Another cause of a
red eye is something

630
00:26:33,970 --> 00:26:35,870
called acute angle
closure glaucoma. This is

631
00:26:35,870 --> 00:26:38,670
a big one for the boards,
both in ophthalmology

632
00:26:38,670 --> 00:26:41,830
and on regular
medical boards, too.

633
00:26:42,390 --> 00:26:46,350
these are patients
that come in with acute

634
00:26:46,350 --> 00:26:49,150
eye pain they say things
got blurry they were

635
00:26:49,150 --> 00:26:51,210
maybe in a dark room
maybe watching a movie

636
00:26:51,210 --> 00:26:54,950
the pain is really
really severe they have

637
00:26:54,950 --> 00:26:58,090
nausea vomiting the eye
is red they have blurry

638
00:26:58,090 --> 00:26:59,870
vision the cornea
looks a little cloudy

639
00:26:59,870 --> 00:27:03,550
and they have a fixed
mid dilated pupil what

640
00:27:04,250 --> 00:27:06,490
happens here is the
space between the cornea

641
00:27:06,490 --> 00:27:08,330
which is the clear outer
covering of the eye

642
00:27:08,330 --> 00:27:10,050
and the iris which is
the colored part of

643
00:27:10,050 --> 00:27:12,630
the eye becomes so
narrow that the aqueous

644
00:27:12,630 --> 00:27:14,530
fluid that normally
flows within the eye to

645
00:27:14,530 --> 00:27:16,770
maintain the eye pressure
gets basically trapped

646
00:27:16,770 --> 00:27:19,810
and so there's nowhere
for the fluid to

647
00:27:19,810 --> 00:27:22,150
go the pressure builds
up and up and up and up

648
00:27:22,150 --> 00:27:24,210
and the patient can
actually be at risk of

649
00:27:24,210 --> 00:27:25,910
vision loss because if
the pressure goes up

650
00:27:25,910 --> 00:27:28,430
really high it can choke
off the blood supply

651
00:27:28,430 --> 00:27:31,050
to the optic nerve so
these patients that

652
00:27:31,050 --> 00:27:34,170
come in the immediate
treatment is to give

653
00:27:34,170 --> 00:27:36,530
eye drops to try to bring
down the eye pressure.

654
00:27:36,530 --> 00:27:39,490
And sometimes IV
acetazolamide and mannitol

655
00:27:39,490 --> 00:27:42,030
can bring down the
eye pressure as well.

656
00:27:42,310 --> 00:27:44,910
And the definitive
treatment is something

657
00:27:44,910 --> 00:27:46,970
called a laser
peripheral iridotomy,

658
00:27:46,970 --> 00:27:49,530
where we make a small
opening in the iris

659
00:27:49,530 --> 00:27:51,890
to allow a new conduit
for the fluid in

660
00:27:51,890 --> 00:27:54,050
the eye to flow through
and to increase the

661
00:27:54,050 --> 00:27:56,210
space between the
cornea and the iris.

662
00:27:56,610 --> 00:27:59,810
So once again, looking at

663
00:27:59,810 --> 00:28:01,510
this acute angle closure,

664
00:28:01,730 --> 00:28:03,670
not conjunctivitis,
a lot of different

665
00:28:03,670 --> 00:28:05,390
kinds of redness
in the eyes.

666
00:28:06,770 --> 00:28:09,550
Definitely
good to be able

667
00:28:09,550 --> 00:28:10,970
to differentiate the two.

668
00:28:11,930 --> 00:28:15,270
Causes of decreased
vision can be as simple

669
00:28:15,270 --> 00:28:17,150
as refractive error.
So needing glasses or

670
00:28:17,150 --> 00:28:19,870
contact lenses, some
patients are myopic,

671
00:28:19,870 --> 00:28:21,370
meaning they're nearsighted.
Some patients are

672
00:28:21,370 --> 00:28:23,330
hyperopic, meaning
they're farsighted. Some

673
00:28:23,330 --> 00:28:26,670
patients have astigmatism,
which just has

674
00:28:26,670 --> 00:28:29,030
to do with the curvature
of the eye. There's

675
00:28:29,030 --> 00:28:31,210
degenerative condition
called keratoconus,

676
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:33,110
where the front part
of the cornea is shaped

677
00:28:33,110 --> 00:28:35,430
more like a cone rather
than a round ball,

678
00:28:35,430 --> 00:28:37,990
which you can see on
the top image there.

679
00:28:38,210 --> 00:28:40,210
And there's also
conditions called

680
00:28:40,210 --> 00:28:42,450
corneal dystrophies,
where there may be

681
00:28:42,450 --> 00:28:44,490
particles or
particulate matter that

682
00:28:44,490 --> 00:28:46,610
is deposited in the
cornea from birth,

683
00:28:46,610 --> 00:28:48,670
which sometimes
causes no problem

684
00:28:48,670 --> 00:28:51,070
with vision, although
many of them do.

685
00:28:51,290 --> 00:28:54,130
You can see that on
the bottom left there.

686
00:28:54,130 --> 00:28:55,260
And then, of course,
we talked about

687
00:28:55,260 --> 00:28:57,110
cataracts as a major
cause of decreased

688
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:59,210
vision in many patients
as we get older.

689
00:29:00,270 --> 00:29:02,270
Another cause of
decreased vision is

690
00:29:02,270 --> 00:29:04,550
glaucoma. So we
talked about acute

691
00:29:04,550 --> 00:29:06,070
angle closure
glaucoma. There's also

692
00:29:06,070 --> 00:29:08,090
something called
open angle glaucoma.

693
00:29:08,090 --> 00:29:10,490
Whatever the cause
of glaucoma, it's

694
00:29:10,490 --> 00:29:12,450
an optic neuropathy.
So what it does

695
00:29:12,450 --> 00:29:14,590
is it hurts the
optic nerve tissue.

696
00:29:14,730 --> 00:29:18,910
So on the top left
there, you see there's

697
00:29:18,910 --> 00:29:20,730
a picture of an optic
nerve that looks very

698
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:23,770
healthy, which is in
picture A and picture

699
00:29:23,770 --> 00:29:26,650
B shows that it's
excavated. So all of that

700
00:29:26,650 --> 00:29:28,510
nerve tissue is gone
because of damage

701
00:29:28,510 --> 00:29:31,790
from glaucoma, which
can cause irreversible

702
00:29:31,790 --> 00:29:34,480
vision loss. There's
also retinal vascular

703
00:29:34,480 --> 00:29:36,270
occlusions that can
occur, which are basically

704
00:29:36,270 --> 00:29:37,910
like mini strokes
to the eye. There

705
00:29:37,910 --> 00:29:40,430
could be branch retinal
artery occlusions. They

706
00:29:40,430 --> 00:29:43,290
could have central
retinal vein inclusions,

707
00:29:43,290 --> 00:29:45,110
which can have a
lot of bleeding and

708
00:29:45,110 --> 00:29:47,250
cause a lot of edema
in the back of the eye.

709
00:29:47,410 --> 00:29:49,050
And of course,
there can also be

710
00:29:49,050 --> 00:29:50,850
retinal detachments,
which can cause

711
00:29:50,850 --> 00:29:52,630
vision loss and
decreased vision.

712
00:29:54,410 --> 00:29:56,770
Another cause of decreased
vision is macular

713
00:29:56,770 --> 00:29:58,470
degeneration or
age-related macular

714
00:29:58,470 --> 00:30:00,790
degeneration or AMD.
There's two different

715
00:30:00,790 --> 00:30:04,070
types of AMD, dry and
wet. The dry kind is

716
00:30:04,070 --> 00:30:06,330
more common, and it's
typically associated

717
00:30:06,330 --> 00:30:08,190
with these little
yellowish-orange

718
00:30:08,190 --> 00:30:10,730
deposits in the back of
the eye called drusen.

719
00:30:10,730 --> 00:30:12,790
For many of these
patients with mild

720
00:30:12,790 --> 00:30:16,030
disease, we follow them.
We recommend taking

721
00:30:16,030 --> 00:30:18,370
different kinds of
antioxidant vitamins.

722
00:30:19,130 --> 00:30:23,290
And many of them do
stabilize. It's very

723
00:30:23,290 --> 00:30:26,290
uncommon for them to
transition over to wet

724
00:30:26,290 --> 00:30:28,870
AMD from dry AMD,
although it can happen.

725
00:30:28,990 --> 00:30:31,670
Wet AMD has to do
with the growth of new

726
00:30:31,670 --> 00:30:33,190
blood vessels in
the back of the eye

727
00:30:33,190 --> 00:30:34,910
and the retina. They
grow through the

728
00:30:34,910 --> 00:30:36,490
retina, they're very
weak and they can cause

729
00:30:36,490 --> 00:30:38,790
bleeding. So these
patients actually

730
00:30:38,790 --> 00:30:40,490
end up getting
injections of medication

731
00:30:40,490 --> 00:30:42,430
in the back of the eye
to cause regression

732
00:30:42,430 --> 00:30:44,430
of those new blood
vessels that grew.

733
00:30:44,830 --> 00:30:46,830
And it also causes
a little bit

734
00:30:46,830 --> 00:30:48,130
of dissipation
of the blood that

735
00:30:48,130 --> 00:30:49,730
in the back of
the eye as well.

736
00:30:49,910 --> 00:30:52,650
And we've come a
long, long way in

737
00:30:52,650 --> 00:30:54,150
terms of the different
amount of therapies

738
00:30:54,150 --> 00:30:56,150
that we have for
